<title>USA: USDA proposes labelling rule for sausage casings.</title>
<headline>USDA proposes labelling rule for sausage casings.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday proposed requiring origin labels for natural sausage casings if they are made from a different type of livestock or poultry than the meat in the sausage.</p>
<p>In a notice in the Federal Register, USDA's Food Safety and Inspection Service said it is also proposing such labels for regenerated collagen casings.</p>
<p>Comments must be received on or before Sept. 15.</p>
</text>
